  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;1.&amp;nbsp;The proposal, by reason of siting and scale,&amp;nbsp;presents an undesirable addition which would cause an unacceptable loss of outlook, daylight and sunlight&amp;nbsp;and an overbearing impact to neighbouring occupiers.&amp;nbsp;This would result in a harmful impact to the amenity currently enjoyed by neighbouring occupiers. As such, the proposal fails to protect residential amenity and constitutes un-neighbourly development. The proposal fails to accord with the following policies which seek to ensure that development proposals protect residential amenity:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policy D6 of the London Plan (March, 2021)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policies DMD1 and DMD5 of&amp;nbsp;The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;"
